{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Those who trust</b> — Rabbi Moses said: it is a participle of the word אירא. This has no meaning. The correct view: הבוטחים is the beginning of the phrase, and the meaning is 'those who trust in their חיל' — their wealth, as in: עשה לי את החיל הזה (Judges 8:2)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:24.857016017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}